    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="12.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VAtr">V Atr</ref> 12.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12.2" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="240" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ealle Godes gerihta fyrðrige man georne, ealswa hit þearf is.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12.2" corresp="#wit-g2"><pb n="240" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ealle Godes gerihta fyrðrige man georne, eallswa hit þearf is.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12.2" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="241" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ealle Godes rihta friðige man georne, ealswa hit þearf is.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="12.2" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="82" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ ealle Godes rihta friðige<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#VAtr_12-2.robnote.fn.6"/> man georne, ealswa hit þearf is.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="150" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ealle Godes gerihta fyrðrige man georne, ealswa hit þearf is.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="241" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_12-2.lnote.de.1"/> alle Kirchengerechtsame fördere (schütze<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VAtr_12-2.lnote.de.2"/> <hi rend="italic">D</hi>) man willig, wie es nöthig ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let all God's dues be eagerly promoted (protected, D), as is needful.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_12-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="83" ed="#robertson"/>And all God's dues shall be promptly rendered<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#VAtr_12-2.robnote.n.2"/>, as the occasion requires.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="449" ed="#whitelock"/>And all God’s dues are to be furthered zealously, as is needful.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="151" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And all God’s dues are to be given willingly, just as is required.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="241"><ref target="clause:EGu_5-1">EGu 5.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. E Gu. 5, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_21-1">VI Atr 21.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares EGu 5.1.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">gerihta fyrðrige: gerihta friðige D</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_12-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">172</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">= VI 21, 1 = VIII 14 = I Cn 14</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">= VI 21, 1 = VIII 14 = I Cn 14</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_12-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">172</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">D's falsche Lesart, auch I Cn 14 A, entstand vielleicht durch die Möglichkeit der Metathesis von <hi rend="italic">frið-</hi> zu <hi rend="italic">firð-</hi>; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Wb: fierdscip, -weard</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">D's false reading, also found in I Cn 14 A, perhaps arose through the possibility of metathesis of <hi rend="italic">frið-</hi> to <hi rend="italic">firð-</hi>; cf. <hi rend="italic">Wb: fierdscip, -weard</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAtr_12-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. E. and G. 5, 1; VI Atr. 21, 1; VIII, 14; I Cn. 14; Wulfstan, pp. 272, 311.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAtr_12-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Is the form in D a case of metathesis?</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="VAtr_12-2.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">82</biblScope></bibl><label>friðige</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gerihta fyrðrige</hi> G, G₂.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
